        // replaces ADMIN_ALERT_EMAIL, CLAIM_ALERT_EMAIL, FOUNDER_ALERT_EMAIL,
        // DATA_QUALITY_EMAIL_TO and ANALYTICS_DIGEST_EMAIL_TO. One address. The
        // analytics and stale-claim digests send from production only, and the
        // data-quality digest from production and demo, whatever this says
        // (`envRule`, lib/notifications/registry.ts).
        "SUPPORT_EMAIL": "support@aecintegrations.com",
        // AECI-241: sender for the daily data-quality digest. Plain var (not a
        // secret). Must be on the Resend-verified sending domain,
        // `aecintegrations.com` (docs/email.md §Deliverability). The recipient is
        // SUPPORT_EMAIL, on production and demo only (AECI-1220).
        "DATA_QUALITY_EMAIL_FROM": "AEC Integrations <notifications@aecintegrations.com>",
        // PUBLIC_SITE_URL is the canonical launch domain — SHARED by transactional
        // email (absolute links in the approved/rejected emails, AECI-240) AND the
        // post-promote IndexNow submission (the origin its URLs are built against,
        // AECI-236 / §20.2; canonicals are self-referential to the serving origin,
        // ADR 0011). Public value. The canonical public host is `www.` (ADR 0011
        // amendment 2026-07-05 — the SSR Worker 301s the bare apex → `www.`), so this
        // matches it: emails and IndexNow emit `www.` URLs that need no redirect hop
        // and agree with the self-referential sitemap `<loc>`s. The launch-only
        // `INDEXNOW_KEY` secret must be provisioned at the same time — the IndexNow
        // ping stays a no-op until it is. (AECI-747 removed the Google Indexing ping:
